    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "542:1925",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Garden",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Garden"
        },
        {
          "text": "My Grandmother's Garden\n\nEvery spring, my grandmother spends her mornings in the garden behind her house. She grows flowers, vegetables, and herbs, and she takes care of everything herself.\n\nThe garden has a small lawn surrounded by a low hedge. Along the fence, there are flower beds full of roses, tulips, and sunflowers. She waters them every morning with a hose or a watering can, depending on how much rain there has been. If the soil is too dry, she uses a sprinkler.\n\nIn the vegetable patch, she plants tomatoes, carrots, lettuce, and peppers. She prepares the soil with a rake and a shovel before planting the seeds. Once the seedlings start to grow, she adds fertiliser and removes any weeds by hand or with a small trowel.\n\nThere is a greenhouse at the back of the garden where she grows herbs like basil and mint all year round. Inside, she keeps pots on wooden shelves and uses a thermometer to check the temperature.\n\nShe also has a compost bin where she puts leftover food and garden waste. After a few months, it turns into rich compost that she mixes into the soil.\n\nMy grandmother says that gardening keeps her active and calm. I enjoy helping her — especially when it is time to pick the ripe vegetables and bring them to the kitchen.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "My Grandmother's Garden Every spring, my grandmother spends her mornings in the garden behind her house. She grows flowers, vegetables, and herbs, and she takes care of everything herself. The garden has a small lawn surrounded by a low hedge. Along the fence, there are flower beds full of roses, tulips, and sunflowers. She waters them every morning with a hose or a watering can, depending on how much rain there has been. If the soil is too dry, she uses a sprinkler. In the vegetable patch, she plants tomatoes, carrots, lettuce, and peppers. She prepares the soil with a rake and a shovel before planting the seeds. Once the seedlings start to grow, she adds fertiliser and removes any weeds by hand or with a small trowel. There is a greenhouse at the back of the garden where she grows herbs like basil and mint all year round. Inside, she keeps pots on wooden shelves and uses a thermometer to check the temperature. She also has a compost bin where she puts leftover food and garden waste. After a few months, it turns into rich compost that she mixes into the soil. My grandmother says that gardening keeps her active and calm. I enjoy helping her — especially when it is time to pick the ripe vegetables and bring them to the kitchen."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. When does the grandmother work in the garden?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. When does the grandmother work in the garden?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. What flowers does she grow along the fence?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. What flowers does she grow along the fence?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. How does she prepare the soil before planting?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. How does she prepare the soil before planting?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. What does she grow in the greenhouse?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. What does she grow in the greenhouse?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. What does the compost bin produce?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "5. What does the compost bin produce?"
        }
      ]
    },
    "idioms-phrases": {
      "nodeId": "542:1938",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases"
        },
        {
          "text": "green thumb / green fingers",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "green thumb / green fingers"
        },
        {
          "text": "natural talent for growing plants",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "natural talent for growing plants"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"My grandmother has a real green thumb — everything she plants grows beautifully.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"My grandmother has a real green thumb — everything she plants grows beautifully.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "nip it in the bud",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "nip it in the bud"
        },
        {
          "text": "stop a problem before it gets worse",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "stop a problem before it gets worse"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"If you see weeds starting, nip them in the bud before they spread.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"If you see weeds starting, nip them in the bud before they spread.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "come up roses",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "come up roses"
        },
        {
          "text": "turn out well, have a good result",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "turn out well, have a good result"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"After all the hard work, the garden came up roses.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"After all the hard work, the garden came up roses.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "dig up",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "dig up"
        },
        {
          "text": "remove from the ground; also: discover information",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "remove from the ground; also: discover information"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"She dug up the old plants to make room for new ones.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"She dug up the old plants to make room for new ones.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "put down roots",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "put down roots"
        },
        {
          "text": "settle in a place and feel at home",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "settle in a place and feel at home"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"After years of moving, they finally put down roots in the countryside.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"After years of moving, they finally put down roots in the countryside.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "grow on someone",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "grow on someone"
